            <ArticleTitle>Gabapentin in phantom limb pain management in children and young adults: report of seven cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>78-82</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Seven children and young adults with phantom limb pain (PLP) were treated with gabapentin. PLP resolved in six patients within two months. One patient still had symptoms to a lesser degree. Mean follow up time was 1.74 years. Gabapentin may be a useful adjunct to pain management in patients with PLP symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
